---
description: Requires a structured report after any implementation, fix, or refactor.
alwaysApply: true
---

After completing any implementation, modification, bug fix, or refactor, ALWAYS provide a structured implementation report.

The report must contain:

1. Modified files

* List every modified/created/deleted file.

2. Exact behavior changes

* Describe only actual user-visible or system-visible behavior changes.
* Do not include assumptions or generic statements.

3. Architecture impact

* Mention:

  * static data shape changes (`data/` JSON or equivalent)
  * JS module / progressive-enhancement contract changes
  * page URL / slug / routing structure changes
  * CSS design-token or shared layout impact
  * SEO markup impact (titles, headings, alt, structured links)
* If none:

  * explicitly state “No architectural changes.”

4. Backward compatibility

* Explain whether existing pages, shared includes/patterns, data files, or UI flows remain compatible.

5. Risks / edge cases

* Mention unresolved risks, limitations, responsive/a11y gaps, content placeholder issues, or known edge cases.

6. Scope discipline validation

* Confirm:

  * no unrelated refactors
  * no parallel systems introduced
  * no architecture redesign unless explicitly requested
  * no accidental production-backend/framework scaffolding

Rules:

* Be concise and factual.
* Do not include code unless explicitly requested.
* Do not omit risks or limitations.
* Do not claim validation/testing that was not actually performed.
